WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.431
Together, Brad Pitt and Angelina Jolie formed
a blazing Hollywood supernova, but now that

00:00:05.431 --> 00:00:09.030
the ultimate celebrity couple has split up,
we're about to find out which half of the

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:12.519
Duo Formerly Known As Brangelina shines the
brightest alone.

00:00:12.519 --> 00:00:16.049
Brad Pitt versus Angelina Jolie: who's the
bigger star?

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:17.591
Round One: Awards

00:00:17.591 --> 00:00:20.640
"And the winner is..."

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:26.800
Jolie's trophy case boasts three Golden Globe
statues for her work in 1997's George Wallace,

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.890
1998's Gia, and 2000's Girl, Interrupted.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:33.950
The latter also earned her a Best Supporting
Actress Oscar and a SAG Award.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.280
Brad Pitt's no awards season slouch, of course.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:41.170
He's got his own Oscar and a BAFTA for his
part as a producer of the 2013 Best Picture

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:46.960
winner 12 Years a Slave, a Golden Globe for
his supporting role in 1995's Twelve Monkeys,

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:52.899
and an Emmy for his work as an executive producer
on the 2014 HBO drama The Normal Heart.

00:00:52.899 --> 00:00:54.360
Advantage: Neither.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:57.930
Both need to build secondary support beams
on their respective prize shelves just to

00:00:57.930 --> 00:00:59.190
hold all their shiny bits.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:01.760
So maybe the real winners here are their contractors.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.250
Round Two: Extracurriculars

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:08.400
It's Angelina's humanitarian accomplishments
outside of acting that really set her apart

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.040
from Brad.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:14.390
In 2001, long before their relationship even
began, she was named to a Goodwill Ambassador

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:18.689
position by the United Nations, after visiting
with Afghan refugees in Pakistan.

00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:23.630
She remained in that role until 2012, when
she was promoted to Special Envoy for the

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:25.880
UN High Commissioner for Refugees.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:30.490
Also in 2001, she began conservation efforts
in Cambodia, which would eventually give her

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.790
secondary citizenship.

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:34.119
It's also where she adopted her son Maddox.

00:01:34.119 --> 00:01:39.180
Other humanitarian awards include an Order
of St. Michael and St. George from Queen Elizabeth

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:44.159
and a Jean Hersholt Humanitarian Award from
the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences.

00:01:44.159 --> 00:01:48.610
To be fair, Pitt did participate in many of
Jolie's overseas efforts over the years, and

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:52.540
his name is right there in the title of the
Jolie-Pitt Foundation they started together

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:53.680
in 2006.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:59.350
Notably, Brad launched the Make It Right Foundation
in 2007, and after Hurricane Katrina left

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:03.590
New Orleans' Ninth Ward in ruins, he courted
investors to rebuild the neighborhood with

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.130
sustainable materials.

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:09.190
Advantage: Jolie's been seen with her boots
on foreign soil as often as she has with her

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:10.709
heels on glitzy red carpets.

00:02:10.709 --> 00:02:14.480
While Pitt's participation doesn't count for
nothing, Jolie definitely has the weightier

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:17.330
name within the international philanthropy
community.

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:19.090
Round Three: Paychecks

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:25.030
It’s basic math: Pitt makes an estimated
$31.5 million annually, while Jolie is said

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:27.550
to bring in roughly half of that, according
to Forbes.

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:31.730
Even their first shared starring vehicle,
Mr. &amp; Mrs. Smith, had a significant rumored

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:36.450
pay discrepancy, with Pitt allegedly pulling
$20 million and Jolie collecting just $10

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:37.920
million for equal screen time.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.950
Though Jolie's had some significant paydays
of her own, ranging up to $20 million for

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:47.470
2010's Salt, Pitt was rumored to make as much
as $30 million for 2001's Ocean's Eleven.

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:51.630
His biggest financial boon, though, comes
by way of his Plan B Entertainment production

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:56.470
company, which has produced films like like
World War Z and The Big Short.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:03:01.080
Add a cool $60 million dollar Netflix deal
to that and the victory is clear.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.550
Advantage: When Pitt gets a spot in front
of the cameras and a seat at the production

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.150
table, it's money in the bank.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:08.750
Round Four: Ticket sales

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:14.760
Jolie's most successful film to date is Disney's
Maleficent, which earned a whopping $758.5

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:16.000
million worldwide.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.520
Pitt's biggest earner was World War Z, which
took in $540 million across the globe.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:24.660
It’s Pitt's only picture to cross the $500
million threshold, but Jolie's got the three

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:27.030
Kung Fu Panda movies to add to her column.

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:31.319
In total, Pitt's movies have made almost $7
billion worldwide, while Jolie's pics are

00:03:31.319 --> 00:03:33.860
closing in on a respectable $6 billion.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:38.670
Interestingly enough, Jolie's reported opening
box office average is just a hair higher,

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:42.310
at around $68 million, while Pitt's is around
$67 million.

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:46.051
Another minor difference is the fact that,
of their top 10 most successful movies, Jolie

00:03:46.051 --> 00:03:50.489
has three that featured her as the singular
central lead—Maleficent, Lara Croft: Tomb

00:03:50.489 --> 00:03:54.769
Raider, and Salt—while Pitt's got two—The
Curious Case of Benjamin Button and World

00:03:54.769 --> 00:03:55.769
War Z.

00:03:55.769 --> 00:03:57.939
Advantage: Jolie, but it's a squeaker.

00:03:57.939 --> 00:04:01.630
Jolie tends to take on projects people are
willing to trek out to theaters to see—and

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:03.980
she does it with just a touch more consistency
than Pitt.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:06.459
"What an awkward situation."

00:04:06.459 --> 00:04:08.950
Round Five: PR skills

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:12.480
Jolie is whip-smart about the fame game, and
there's plenty of proof.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.190
Consider the time when she penned her own
harrowing op-eds in the New York Times about

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:20.690
getting a double mastectomy and then a hysterectomy,
after managing to avoid the paparazzi long

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:22.930
enough to actually have these treatments done.

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:26.980
And then there’s the way she started capitalizing
on the tabloid value of her private life—like

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:31.050
photos of her newborn children or wedding
dress—to turn that into easy money made

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:32.050
for charity.

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:36.250
Pitt, meanwhile, tends to keep a lower profile
with the media instead of using it to his

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:37.250
advantage.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:38.410
Advantage: Jolie.

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:40.580
By a mile.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.800
Round Six: Sex appeal

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:47.639
Both Jolie and Pitt earned a significant amount
of their initial fame based on their devastatingly

00:04:47.639 --> 00:04:48.639
good looks.

00:04:48.639 --> 00:04:51.960
Check out Pitt in Fight Club or his extra-toned
chest in Troy.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:53.830
How about Jolie’s bath scene in Wanted?

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:55.370
It’s a scientific fact.

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:58.250
They’re considered some of the world's most
attractive humans.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:01.520
Advantage: They're both hot, and they both
know it, but Pitt gets the advantage as a

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:03.750
two-time "Sexiest Man Alive."

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:06.190
Round Seven: The endorsements

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:11.240
Jolie nabbed a massive $10 million ad deal
to prop Louis Vuitton, which is why she seems

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:13.620
to always have one of the fashion house's
bags in hand.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:18.470
Pitt, meanwhile, scored $7 million to make
a laughably awful commercial for Chanel No.

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:23.669
5 and added another $3 million to his stacks
for a Cadillac ad that only ran in China.

00:05:23.669 --> 00:05:26.900
Advantage: Pitt might be the more frequent
flyer in the ad lane…

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:29.020
(Pringles commercial song playing)

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:32.370
...but when Jolie does it, she goes BIG.

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:33.720
The tally

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:34.820
It's really close.

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:38.600
Jolie's got some serious mainstream muster,
thanks to her fascinating image overhaul.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:42.400
She’s no longer "that weird girl who made
out with her brother", but instead that rare

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.009
celebrity who actually uses her fame for good.

00:05:45.009 --> 00:05:48.970
People can't seem to look away, and not just
because of her unique beauty; she's smart,

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:50.740
strategic, and makes it worth the watch.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:53.470
That said, Pitt's been Mr. Popularity for
ages.

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:57.080
It's not just that he's always been chummy
with some of Hollywood's chillest A-listers,

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:00.150
or even the fact that he’s name checked
in a pop-country song.

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:05.279
"Ok, so you're Brad Pitt...that don't impress
me much."

00:06:05.279 --> 00:06:09.410
Jolie might be able to run a room by talking
about important issues, but people will gravitate

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:11.630
toward Pitt to hear him read the phone book.

00:06:11.630 --> 00:06:15.150
Pitt was already fully established before
he and Jolie started all the Brangelunacy

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:18.100
11 years ago, and that's what gives him the
win here.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:19.330
He got here first.

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:20.580
It's as simple as that.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.100
Victory Brad.

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:22.840
So, Angelina...

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:28.540
"That's what losing sounds like."

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:29.710
Thanks for watching!

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:33.669
